Encryption 🔒

Definition:
Encryption means converting readable data into a secret code so that unauthorized people cannot read it.

Example

Without Encryption:

Password:
123456

Anyone can read it.

With Encryption:

Password:
A8x#K9Lp$2

Only the system with the correct key can decrypt it.

Real-life Example

Sending money through a banking app uses encryption to protect your account details.

One-Line Answer

Encryption protects sensitive data by converting it into an unreadable format that only authorized users or systems can access.
